\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, all-atoning Lamb,
\par Thine, and only Thine, I am:
\par Take my body, spirit, soul;
\par Only Thou possess the whole.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou may one thing needful be;
\par Let me ever cleave to Thee;
\par Let me choose the better part;
\par Let me give Thee all my heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Fairer than the sons men,
\par Do not let me turn again,
\par Leave the fountain-head of bliss,
\par Stoop to creature-happiness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Whom have I on earth below?
\par Thee, and only Thee, I know;
\par Whom have I in heaven but Thee?
\par Thou art in all to me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. All my treasure is above,
\par All my riches is Thy love;
\par Who the worth of love can tell?
\par Infinite, unsearchable.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

